contentText:
Ahead of the arrival of Charli xcx&rsquo;s new album Music, Fashion, Film , the British pop star revealed the LP&rsquo;s tracklist via social media on Tuesday (July 7).

&ldquo;My new album Music, Fashion, Film is out july 24th. 11 songs, 30 minutes, 5 seconds. available to pre order now, love you xx,&rdquo; she wrote on Instagram alongside a photo of her holding a T-shirt with the album&rsquo;s tracklist. There&rsquo;s a lone guest appearance on the album&rsquo;s closer, &ldquo;No One Lasts Forever,&rdquo; from film director David Cronenberg.

Music, Fashion, Film serves as Charli&rsquo;s seventh studio album. The project includes previously released singles &ldquo;SS26,&rdquo; &ldquo;Wink Wink&rdquo; and &ldquo;Rock Music.&rdquo; Charli is set to host 25 Music, Fashion Film listening parties in select cities across the world later this week, from July 9 through July 11. Taking place at indie movie theaters, the North American screenings include New York City, Boston, Atlanta, Los Angeles, Chicago, Boston, Miami, Phoenix, Seattle, Denver, Toronto and Santa Cruz, Calif.&nbsp;

Outside of North America, there are global screenings slated for London; Manchester, England; S&atilde;o Paulo; Mexico City; Madrid; Milan; Brussels; Amsterdam; Dublin; Paris; Berlin; Sydney; Melbourne, Australia; Auckland, New Zealand; and Tokyo.

Following MFF &lsquo;s arrival, Charli will hit the road for a North American arena tour, which is set to kick off in Philadelphia on Sept. 11.

Charli xcx took the pop world by storm with her blockbuster album Brat in June 2024, which reached No. 3 on the Billboard 200 , her highest charting LP in the U.S. to date.

